WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:00.619
perfectly.

00:00:00.752 --> 00:00:02.921
&gt;&gt; We're still trying to figure

00:00:03.055 --> 00:00:04.790
out what some of these things

00:00:04.923 --> 00:00:06.258
were, and they were not in the

00:00:06.391 --> 00:00:06.892
category of the balloon.

00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:09.127
&gt;&gt; Let's bring in Gordon Chang,

00:00:09.261 --> 00:00:10.529
an analyst on China and north

00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:11.196
Korea.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.297
Good to see you.

00:00:12.431 --> 00:00:15.934
You said you think Russia could

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:16.568
possibly also be involved with

00:00:16.702 --> 00:00:17.569
these objects.

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:19.338
You tweeted last night, "We will

00:00:19.471 --> 00:00:20.839
be in the fight soon.

00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:22.441
China and Russia are making sure

00:00:22.574 --> 00:00:24.409
that we're at the end of decades

00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:26.044
of general peace."

00:00:26.178 --> 00:00:27.946
That's a terrifying proposition.

00:00:27.946 --> 00:00:29.348
We still don't know what those

00:00:29.481 --> 00:00:30.882
other three objects were, and

00:00:31.016 --> 00:00:32.684
there's a chance we might never

00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:32.985
know.

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:36.455
Do you really think that this

00:00:36.588 --> 00:00:38.657
could kick off nonstop conflict

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.360
if not World War III?

00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:43.629
&gt;&gt; That's a possibility, Jake.

00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:45.230
Remember, the objects that were

00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:48.200
shot down on Friday and Saturday

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.635
entered North American air space

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:50.302
from the north.

00:00:50.435 --> 00:00:52.104
And that means that they

00:00:52.237 --> 00:00:55.207
probably passed over Russia.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.475
That means perhaps Russia --

00:00:56.608 --> 00:00:58.076
these are Russian objects, maybe

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.345
China launched them from Russia,

00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:01.980
or maybe China launched them

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.548
from China, but they floated

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:06.218
over Russia, which means that

00:01:06.351 --> 00:01:07.019
Russia presumably gave approval

00:01:07.152 --> 00:01:08.820
to them.

00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:10.656
We know that China's top

00:01:10.789 --> 00:01:11.990
diplomat is going to be in

00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:13.325
Moscow in a couple days.

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.994
That follows by a couple weeks

00:01:15.994 --> 00:01:17.262
the vice foreign minister going

00:01:17.396 --> 00:01:19.564
to Moscow.

00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:21.066
XI jinping, the Chinese ruler,

00:01:21.199 --> 00:01:22.134
is supposed to go to the Moscow

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.036
this year, and we've seen China

00:01:24.169 --> 00:01:25.404
be all in on the Russian war

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:26.204
effort in Ukraine.

00:01:26.338 --> 00:01:28.040
So, the conclusion is that China

00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:30.275
and Russia are forming a durable

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:30.676
partnership.

00:01:30.809 --> 00:01:36.014
&gt;&gt; And what are these objects,

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:36.214
do you think?

00:01:36.348 --> 00:01:36.848
Do you think they're just

00:01:36.982 --> 00:01:38.784
provocative, they're trying to

00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:39.418
needle us, surveillance,

00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:40.018
potentially weapons?

00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:43.355
&gt;&gt; We don't know.

00:01:43.488 --> 00:01:45.590
Apparently they were smaller so

00:01:46.024 --> 00:01:46.591
they might be less dangerous

00:01:46.725 --> 00:01:48.026
than the balloon that entered

00:01:48.026 --> 00:01:50.262
into the usair space on January

00:01:50.395 --> 00:01:51.263
28th from the south, which was

00:01:51.396 --> 00:01:53.365
Chinese.

00:01:53.498 --> 00:01:54.166
We don't know.

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:57.235
And as you heard from those

00:01:57.369 --> 00:01:59.671
senators who attended a

00:02:00.038 --> 00:02:00.339
briefing, I don't think the

00:02:00.472 --> 00:02:01.573
administration knows either.

00:02:01.707 --> 00:02:03.008
But one thing, I think president

00:02:03.141 --> 00:02:05.577
Biden needs to address the

00:02:05.711 --> 00:02:06.311
American public.

00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:08.046
Even if we don't know.

00:02:08.046 --> 00:02:09.181
And the American people need to

00:02:09.314 --> 00:02:11.616
hear it from our leader.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:12.984
You know, Canada's Justin

00:02:13.118 --> 00:02:14.820
Trudeau spoke to Canada about

00:02:14.953 --> 00:02:17.022
the object that was over their

00:02:17.155 --> 00:02:17.356
country.

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:19.491
President Biden needs to do the

00:02:19.624 --> 00:02:20.058
same thing.

00:02:20.158 --> 00:02:21.393
&gt;&gt; I want to get your take on

00:02:21.526 --> 00:02:23.595
how the U.S. Is handling this in

00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:25.030
terms of communication with the

00:02:25.163 --> 00:02:28.266
Chinese leaders.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:28.967
Obviously, secretary of state

00:02:29.101 --> 00:02:30.068
Antony blinken canceled his trip

00:02:30.068 --> 00:02:32.304
to China after that first

00:02:32.437 --> 00:02:34.072
Chinese spy balloon.

00:02:34.072 --> 00:02:37.676
We're told that the ministry of

00:02:38.076 --> 00:02:40.545
defense in China has not taken

00:02:40.679 --> 00:02:42.147
calls from secretary of defense

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.383
Austin or other attempts at

00:02:44.516 --> 00:02:46.084
outreach, and the state

00:02:46.084 --> 00:02:47.486
department spokesman Ned price

00:02:47.619 --> 00:02:48.687
said yesterday the U.S. Believes

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.389
in keeping lines of

00:02:50.522 --> 00:02:52.290
communication open with China.

00:02:52.424 --> 00:02:52.858
How should the Biden

00:02:52.991 --> 00:02:53.558
administration be addressing

00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:54.126
this when it comes to

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:57.162
communication with China?

00:02:57.295 --> 00:02:58.663
&gt;&gt; I don't think we should be

00:02:58.797 --> 00:03:00.098
talking to China.

00:03:00.098 --> 00:03:00.932
China right now is not in a

00:03:01.066 --> 00:03:03.168
position to deal with the united

00:03:03.301 --> 00:03:05.103
States in good faith, and so I

00:03:05.237 --> 00:03:06.938
don't see why we should be

00:03:07.072 --> 00:03:08.140
communicating with them.

00:03:08.273 --> 00:03:14.112
You know, it's an article of

00:03:14.112 --> 00:03:15.013
faith among Americans that you

00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:18.183
talk to an adversary, talk to an

00:03:18.316 --> 00:03:18.483
enemy.

00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:20.485
But by doing that, we've

00:03:20.619 --> 00:03:22.254
emboldened the worst elements in

00:03:22.387 --> 00:03:24.122
Chinese political system by

00:03:24.122 --> 00:03:24.623
showing that bridge rant acts

00:03:24.756 --> 00:03:26.725
are able to get the united

00:03:26.858 --> 00:03:28.126
States to a position where we

00:03:28.193 --> 00:03:30.762
look like we're desperately

00:03:30.896 --> 00:03:31.496
trying to pursue China.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.632
We heard president Biden in that

00:03:33.765 --> 00:03:36.134
conversation with pbs say, well,

00:03:36.134 --> 00:03:38.136
this incident, this spy balloon

00:03:38.136 --> 00:03:40.305
incident, is not going to change

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:41.573
u.s./china relations.

00:03:41.706 --> 00:03:42.808
Essentially, that was telling

00:03:42.941 --> 00:03:44.209
China there's going to be no

00:03:44.342 --> 00:03:46.144
cost for what was obviously a

00:03:46.178 --> 00:03:46.778
very dangerous act.

00:03:46.912 --> 00:03:48.513
So we need to have a new way of

